Inventory Levels, at 52.8, decreased 2.2%, expanding, at a slower rate, with the report noting that the reading is “close to no movement”;
 Inventory Costs, at 78.6, increased 1.6%, expanding, at a slower rate, marking the second-fastest rate of expansion in 12 months, with the report noting that Inventory Cost expansion is now outstripping the growth rate in Inventory Levels by 25.8%, nearly double to average delta of 13.1% between the two metrics;
 Warehousing Capacity, at 53.5, up 7.2%, expanding, after contracting in July, for its fastest rate of expansion on a year-to-date basis;
